session:pr424Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #363 tracks a series of panic-removal PRs across rdf_owl_translator; PR #418 had already threaded TranslatorError through most call chains, leaving three panics whose enclosing functions were already Result-returning: topological_sort (ingress.rs) panicking on a cyclic anonymous-class-expression dependency graph, and two axiom_parser.rs sites panicking on a subject with more than one owl:members triple under owl:AllDisjointClasses/owl:AllDisjointProperties. This PR was picked up mid-flight after the originally-delegated sub-agent was interrupted by the account's monthly API spend limit, with its edits already sitting uncommitted in the worktree. Rather than re-delegate or discard the work, reviewed the existing diff against the plan doc (docs/plans/CLASS_EXPR_CYCLE_AND_DISJOINT_MEMBERS_363_PLAN.md) line by line -- new CyclicDependency/MultipleOwlMembers TranslatorError variants matching the established enum style, topological_sort's signature changed to return Result with its one caller (parse_anonymous_exprs) updated via a one-line '?', both axiom_parser.rs panics replaced with Err returns, and matching unit/integration tests including a genuine two-blank-node cyclic owl:intersectionOf fixture exercised through the real rdf2owl entry point rather than just the internal function -- confirmed it matched the plan's design faithfully before trusting it. A forced rebuild (touching the changed files to defeat the shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR staleness hazard) and the full quality gate (fmt, clippy --workspace, cargo test --workspace) were run independently rather than trusting any prior self-report. This surfaced one real problem the interrupted sub-agent had not reached: tests/owl_integration.rs had a pre-existing non-exhaustive match on TranslatorError that the new variants broke, fixed with a single wildcard arm. try_get_individual/try_get_literal (9 call sites, some inside non-Result-returning closures) were deliberately left out of scope as a further #363 follow-up, so this PR does not close the issue." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:424 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr424 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
